  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, does not demonstrate that the development is safe from flooding and will not increase flood risk elsewhere. In the absence of an adequate flood risk assessment and sustainable drainage strategy, the proposal fails to demonstrate how proposed measures manage the risk of flooding and utilise  Sustainable Urban Drainage Systems (SuDS) following the drainage hierarchy in the London Plan, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan (2021), CP21 and CP28 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD59, DMD60, DMD61, DMD62 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the Enfield Strategic Flood Risk Assessment (2021).\r",
    "The proposed ground floor arrangement would not result in a satisfactory layout by virtue of the lack of adequate functional communal space which would be disturbed by the passage of bicycles directly via the only communal space to be provided and the inclusion of ground floor bedrooms in an area at risk of flooding. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policies D6, T2, T5, SI12 and SI13 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy 25 of Core Strategy (2010),  Policies DMD 5, DMD 8, DMD 47, DMD 59, DMD 61 and DMD 62 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the siting of cycle parking within the rear garden and obstructed access route via the ground floor kitchen area, would fail to provide cycle parking provision in line with London Plan standards and would be prohibitive to the promotion of cycling as both a healthy and sustainable form of transport, contrary to Policies DMD 5, DMD 8 and DMD 47 of the Development Management Document (2014), Policies T2 and T5 of the London Plan (2021) and Core Policy 25 of Core Strategy (2010).\r\r"
  ],
